🎯 Project Goal and Real-World Application

The primary goal of this simulation was to systematically identify and ethically exploit the 10 most critical web application security risks, as defined by the OWASP Foundation.

This project directly simulates the tasks of an Application Security (AppSec) Engineer or a Web Penetration Tester, showing proficiency in:
Vulnerability Assessment: Identifying flaws in source code and application logic.
Exploitation: Demonstrating the impact of the flaws using common attack techniques.
Mitigation: Providing targeted, actionable recommendations to developers and engineers.

